From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:01:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ptyd: an interrupt character typed in raw mode starts its own
 packet

In raw mode ptyd hands a reader one packet per read, and the bytes of one
input write form one packet. On the Pi's serial console getty is often
still writing the line editor's output when Enter and a Ctrl-C right after
it arrive, so it forwards both in one write. Ion's line editor (liner,
through the buffered stdin) then reads them in one read: the Ctrl-C stays
in its buffer, never becomes SIGINT, and the program runs on. Pi test 219:
3 of 10 Ctrl-Cs 0.01-0.03 s after Enter were lost.

With ISIG off, an interrupt character now starts a new packet. The read
that ends the line leaves it in ptyd, and isig_enabled() turns it into
SIGINT once the editor switches ISIG back on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ptyd/src/pty.rs | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ptyd/src/pty.rs b/ptyd/src/pty.rs
index 4695cca..2a1cf20 100644
--- a/ptyd/src/pty.rs
+++ b/ptyd/src/pty.rs
@@ -211,6 +211,23 @@ impl Pty {
                 }
             }
 
+            // ISIG off, raw mode (a line editor): an interrupt character
+            // starts a packet of its own, so the read that takes the line
+            // before it does not take it too. isig_enabled() turns it into
+            // SIGINT when the line editor switches ISIG back on. Without
+            // this, an Enter and a Ctrl-C forwarded in one write (getty on a
+            // busy serial console) end up in the editor's buffer together.
+            if !isig
+                && !icanon
+                && usize::from(cc[VMIN]) <= 1
+                && is_cc(b, VINTR)
+                && !is_vdisable(VINTR)
+                && !self.cooked.is_empty()
+            {
+                self.mosi.push_back(self.cooked.clone());
+                self.cooked.clear();
+            }
+
             if ixon {
                 if is_cc(b, VSTART) {
                     println!("VSTART");
